414|# each site read-only and returns one finding per mismatch, named by path + JSON pointer.
415|#
416|# debt[] entries are live sites that do NOT yet agree with the registry but are recorded as known
417|# debt (e.g. the legacy AppData binding in config/hermes.json). They are reported by check_drift as
418|# the typed code PROJECTION_DEBT (warn severity) rather than DRIFT_VALUE, so the drift gate stays a
419|# truthful hard-fail on the reproducibility sites (registry source + sealed lane) while not
420|# pretending the migration is already done. Debt is never a PASS proxy.
